## Typed FFI return surface (docs/specs/types/typed_ffi_returns.spec.md).
## All non-Int-shaped returns lifted: `.new` -> SharedSync[T] with T
## inferred from the constructor's first arg (B1+B3); `.clone` ->
## SharedSync[T] (B5: Self in return); `.get` -> T (B4).
## `SharedSync[T: Send]` — the payload must be `Send` to be shared across
## threads. Feature B (generic trait-bound enforcement) checks this bound
## at the `SharedSync.new(value)` construction site (E1102), replacing the
## old hardcoded `concurrency.rs` Send check.
class SharedSync[T: Send]
  include Send

  include Sync

  lib "runtime/sharedsync.c"
    def self.new as "ruxen_sharedsync_new"(initial: T) -> SharedSync[T]
    def clone as "ruxen_sharedsync_clone" -> SharedSync[T]
    def strong_count as "ruxen_sharedsync_strong_count" -> Int
    def get as "ruxen_sharedsync_get" -> T
    def drop as "ruxen_sharedsync_drop" -> nil
  end
end
